@page "/docs/components/theme-switcher"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.ThemeSwitcher
<PageTitle>Theme Switcher - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Theme Switcher</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="theme-switcher" />
        </div>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">Three ready-made pickers for the light / dark / system preference: a segmented switcher, a menu-embeddable radio group, and a one-button toggle. All of them talk to the same theme module (persisted to <code>localStorage</code>, re-applied pre-paint by <code>boot.js</code>), and every switcher on the page stays in sync - change one and the rest follow, including the OS flipping while in system mode. How the underlying tokens work is covered in <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="docs/theming">Theming</a>.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(ThemeSwitcherExample)" />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Segmented switcher" Description="Shows the persisted preference - system, light, dark. Try it against the one in this site's header: they move together."
          Example="typeof(ThemeSwitcherExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Without the system option" Description="ShowSystem=false hides the follow-the-OS option when you only want an explicit light/dark choice."
          Example="typeof(ThemeSwitcherNoSystemExample)" />

    <Demo Title="In a menu" Description="BzThemeMenu is a radio group of menu items - embed it in any dropdown, like a profile menu."
          Example="typeof(ThemeMenuExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Single toggle" Description="BzThemeToggle flips between light and dark - it shows what is on screen now and switches to the opposite (from system it lands on an explicit choice)."
          Example="typeof(ThemeToggleExample)" />

    <ApiReference Types="ApiFamilies.ThemeSwitcher" />
</div>
